menu "espOS core"

    config ESPOS_CORE_HEALTH_WATCHDOG
        bool "Restart on health conditions the device cannot recover from"
        default y
        help
            When on, espos_init() arms espos_health's watchdog policy: the
            device restarts after three consecutive 10 s ticks with a
            condition in ALARM that was reported with
            ESPOS_HEALTH_F_REBOOT_ON_ALARM (internal RAM exhausted, the
            SignalK stream dead for sk.stall_s while WiFi is up, a watched
            task stalled). A WiFi loss never counts. The per-app
            espos_start_opts_t.health_watchdog can still turn it off at
            runtime. Details: docs/health.md.

            Turn it off for a device whose application handles such
            conditions itself, or where a restart would be worse than the
            condition (a display mid-passage).

endmenu
